1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:04,940
Hi, It's time to talk about job interview.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:08,150
Online and offline interview.

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:12,050
I will give you a lot of tips for interview.

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,640
Okay.

5
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:19,100
So two main types of interviews nowadays are online interview.

6
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:27,410
We are platforms like Zoom or Google meets and offline interview, also known as in-person or on site

7
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:28,230
interview.

8
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:33,710
For this type of interview, you need to actually come to companies office.

9
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,060
All right.

10
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:38,440
Rolls on the interview.

11
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:45,790
People asking the questions and checking the candidate are called interviewers.

12
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:51,010
Candidate who is being interviewed is called Interviewee.

13
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:59,050
So here on the picture, we can see three interviewers interviewing an interviewee.

14
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:00,790
All right.

15
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:05,140
General tips for any type of interview.

16
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:06,660
Arrive on time.

17
00:01:06,670 --> 00:01:07,960
Don't be late.

18
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:10,090
Dress smartly.

19
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:16,450
Do research about the company in advance and speak clearly.

20
00:01:16,990 --> 00:01:21,400
Don't talk bad about your former boss or company.

21
00:01:21,430 --> 00:01:24,010
Don't avoid eye contact.

22
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:29,410
Don't reply only yes or no and do not tell lies.

23
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:30,580
All right.

24
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:35,230
Tips for online interview.

25
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:37,900
Choose a nice background.

26
00:01:37,990 --> 00:01:42,520
Your interviewers don't need to see your messy room.

27
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:45,540
Eliminate background noise.

28
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:50,290
That means find a quiet place for your interview.

29
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:52,720
Turn on your camera.

30
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:58,510
Your interviewers have to see your face and you should have an eye contact with them.

31
00:01:58,990 --> 00:02:01,420
Test your devices in advance.

32
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:03,940
Check if everything works.

33
00:02:03,970 --> 00:02:10,420
Your camera, your laptop, your headphones and work on your lighting.

34
00:02:10,450 --> 00:02:13,210
Choose the well-lit spot.

35
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:14,650
All right.

36
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:23,290
So basically there are only two main types of questions during the interview.

37
00:02:23,590 --> 00:02:30,760
Type one What value can you add to my company as an employee and can you prove it?

38
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,720
So.

39
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:41,770
Interviewer wants to know why do we need to hire you so they can ask questions like, What is your greatest

40
00:02:41,770 --> 00:02:42,880
achievement?

41
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:46,270
What are your strengths and weaknesses?

42
00:02:46,990 --> 00:02:52,030
Second type of questions Why do you want this job?

43
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:57,790
So interviewer wants to find out what is your motivation?

44
00:02:58,510 --> 00:03:03,370
So why do you actually want to work for this company?

45
00:03:03,370 --> 00:03:09,910
And they can ask you questions like, Why do you want to leave your present job?

46
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:12,090
All right.

47
00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:18,520
What to do if you did not understand the question.

48
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,980
Never try to answer a question that you did not understand.

49
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:29,050
And don't say words like say again or what?

50
00:03:29,350 --> 00:03:31,330
That sounds rude.

51
00:03:31,970 --> 00:03:36,350
Instead ask interviewer to repeat.

52
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:42,770
You can use sentences like, I'm sorry, could you please repeat that?

53
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,650
I didn't quite catch that.

54
00:03:45,770 --> 00:03:47,960
Can you ask again, please?

55
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,680
Excuse me.

56
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:52,790
I'm not sure I understood entirely.

57
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,590
Forgive me.

58
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:58,070
I didn't quite understand the last question.

59
00:03:58,580 --> 00:03:59,990
So sorry.

60
00:04:00,020 --> 00:04:03,500
Would you mind repeating that last question, please?

61
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:08,500
Pause the video and repeat these sentences.

62
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:10,720
Good job.

63
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,280
What to say?

64
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:16,090
If you need more time to answer the question.

65
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:19,390
You can say that's a great question.

66
00:04:19,390 --> 00:04:25,450
Let me think about that or let me think about that for a second.

67
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:28,870
I need a moment to think about that.

68
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:33,010
Pause the video and repeat the sentences.

69
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:35,480
Good.

70
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:43,670
At the end of an interview, an interviewer might ask you, Do you have any questions for us?

71
00:04:44,510 --> 00:04:48,350
So bad examples of questions to ask.

72
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:52,580
Tell me more about your company or how much money will I get?

73
00:04:52,610 --> 00:04:55,630
Do not ask these questions.

74
00:04:55,640 --> 00:05:03,590
Instead, you can ask What do you think is the most challenging aspect of this role?

75
00:05:03,950 --> 00:05:07,940
What are the next steps in the hiring process?

76
00:05:08,090 --> 00:05:14,150
What opportunities are there for professional development within your company?

77
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:22,400
These questions show that you are interested in the role and that you are enthusiastic.

78
00:05:22,790 --> 00:05:27,380
Pause the video and repeat these questions.

79
00:05:28,610 --> 00:05:29,840
Nicely done.

80
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:33,620
Okay, Some more secret tips for you guys.

81
00:05:33,710 --> 00:05:36,630
Be open during a job interview.

82
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:37,740
Smile.

83
00:05:37,830 --> 00:05:41,520
Be professional, but don't be very serious.

84
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:46,170
Remember, you and your interviewer are people, not robots.

85
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:48,930
All right, that's it.

86
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:50,700
Thank you.

87
00:05:50,730 --> 00:05:54,090
More practice in your file by.
